<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#ebony">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ebony</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ebony is a dense, dark hardwood from tropical <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> that was highly valued as a luxury material in the ancient world. It was among the goods that moved from the African interior to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, appearing in the trade of the Egyptian Empire <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hatshepsut">Hatshepsut</a>'s expedition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/land-of-punt">Punt</a>, and in the commerce of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushite-empire">Kushite Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ebony.jpg" alt="Ebony" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: OboeCrack · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C3%89bano.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
